---
import ContentPage from '../../components/ContentPage.astro';
import FAQ from '../../components/FAQ.astro';

const faqItems = [
  { question: 'What should I buy first?', answer: 'Prioritize ingredients needed by the current menu, then spend remaining Cash on equipment, furniture, or decorations that fit your next upgrade.' },
  { question: 'What if an item is not available?', answer: 'Recheck the shop later and keep enough Cash ready for the item you need. Use an available alternative only if it still supports your current plan.' },
  { question: 'How much Cash should I keep?', answer: 'There is no single amount for every restaurant. Keep enough to restock the ingredients used by your current menu before planning optional upgrades.' },
];
---
<ContentPage title="Karinderya Shop Restock Guide" description="Plan grocery, furniture, and equipment purchases around the current Karinderya shop inventory." kicker="Planning guide" intro="A practical guide to checking stock and planning purchases." parent={{ label: 'Guides', href: '/guides/' }} relatedLinks={[{ label: 'Grocery', href: '/grocery/' }, { label: 'Ingredients', href: '/ingredients/' }, { label: 'Furniture', href: '/furniture/' }, { label: 'Equipment', href: '/equipment/' }]} sourceIds={['codex-menu', 'wiki-furniture', 'wiki-money']} tableOfContents>
  <h2 id="shop-overview">Shop Overview</h2>
  <p>Karinderya includes grocery inventory, furniture, and equipment listings. Availability and values may change as the game receives updates.</p>

  <h2 id="restock-planning">Restock Planning</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Review the ingredients used by the current menu.</li>
    <li>Check the Grocery before stock becomes too low for upcoming orders.</li>
    <li>Buy essential ingredients before optional furniture or decoration upgrades.</li>
    <li>Keep some Cash available when waiting for a needed item to return.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="purchase-priorities">Purchase Priorities</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Ingredients:</strong> protect the restaurant's ability to complete current orders.</li>
    <li><strong>Equipment:</strong> address cooking delays or limited station capacity.</li>
    <li><strong>Furniture:</strong> improve the dining area when service and stocking are stable.</li>
    <li><strong>Decorations:</strong> customize the restaurant after essential needs are covered.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="shopping-tips">Shopping Tips</h2>
  <p>Use the <a href="/grocery/">Grocery page</a> to compare ingredient listings, then visit the Furniture and Equipment sections before spending on restaurant upgrades.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Check the displayed price again before confirming a purchase.</li>
    <li>Avoid spending the full Cash balance on one optional upgrade.</li>
    <li>Plan around the restaurant's current bottleneck rather than buying every available item.</li>
  </ul>

  <FAQ items={faqItems} />
</ContentPage>
